{"slug":"ops-prod-ops","title":"Production operations","blocks":[{"id":"b1","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Production environment (canonical)"},{"id":"b2","type":"table","head":[[{"type":"text","value":"Fact"}],[{"type":"text","value":"Value"}]],"rows":[[[{"type":"text","value":"Host"}],[{"type":"text","value":"89.167.28.206","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" — Hetzner cax11, ARM64 (aarch64), Ubuntu 22.04"}]],[[{"type":"text","value":"App dir"}],[{"type":"text","value":"/opt/barkpark","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (server tracks "},{"type":"text","value":"origin/main","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"core.hooksPath=.githooks","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":")"}]],[[{"type":"text","value":"Service"}],[{"type":"text","value":"systemd "},{"type":"text","value":"barkpark.service","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"; wrapper "},{"type":"text","value":"api/start.sh","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (sources ASDF + "},{"type":"text","value":".env","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":")"}]],[[{"type":"text","value":"Proxy"}],[{"type":"text","value":"Caddy on :80 → the "},{"type":"text","value":"/etc/caddy/Caddyfile","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" upstream ("},{"type":"text","value":":4000","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" here, 4000↔4001 on "},{"type":"text","value":".slots","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":") — read it; smoke by the PUBLIC URL"}]],[[{"type":"text","value":"Erlang/Elixir"}],[{"type":"text","value":"via ASDF (Erlang Solutions has no ARM packages)"}]],[[{"type":"text","value":"Go"}],[{"type":"text","value":"/usr/local/go/bin/go","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (official ARM64 binary)"}]],[[{"type":"text","value":"Env file"}],[{"type":"text","value":"/opt/barkpark/.env","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"text","value":"DATABASE_URL","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"SECRET_KEY_BASE","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"BARKPARK_EXTRA_ORIGINS","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" ws origins)"}]],[[{"type":"text","value":"Logs"}],[{"type":"text","value":"journalctl $U -f","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"text","value":"$U","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" = all three units)"}]]]},{"id":"b3","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Deploy: "},{"type":"text","value":"ssh root@89.167.28.206","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"cd /opt/barkpark","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"git pull","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (post-merge hook auto-rebuilds + restarts) or "},{"type":"text","value":"make deploy","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":". Golden Rules apply verbatim — never partial-clean "},{"type":"text","value":"_build","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", never skip "},{"type":"text","value":"systemctl restart","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", always test after deploy."}]},{"id":"b4","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"The postcheck rule"},{"id":"b5","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"A misbooted or stopped Phoenix node looks identical to a healthy one from outside — systemd returned, SSH closed, nothing surfaced. So any workflow touching "},{"type":"text","value":"systemctl barkpark","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" on prod "},{"type":"text","value":"must","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" end with "},{"type":"text","value":"api/scripts/prod-postcheck.sh","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", which probes the public HTTP surface."}]},{"id":"b6","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"type":"text","value":"Atomic transitions:","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" prefer "},{"type":"text","value":"systemctl restart","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" to stop-then-start (document a deliberate stop), and a Makefile target to ad-hoc "},{"type":"text","value":"systemctl","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"."}],[{"type":"text","value":"No silent ops:","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" SSH’d in to patch something? Run the script before you log out; refuse “looks fine, didn’t check.”"}]]},{"id":"b7","type":"code","value":"ssh root@<prod-host> \"cd /opt/barkpark && ./api/scripts/prod-postcheck.sh\"\n# QUOTED, or the cd runs on your laptop. On the box: drop the ssh."},{"id":"b8","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"It runs "},{"type":"text","value":"systemctl is-active --quiet barkpark","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", STARTING an inactive service — a guardrail, not a monitor: run it only when “should be running” is the desired end state; sleeps 2 s for the BEAM to bind its port; then requires HTTP 200 from "},{"type":"text","value":"/api/schemas","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (unauth JSON — swap to "},{"type":"text","value":"/studio","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" if retired, never admin-gated "},{"type":"text","value":"/v1/schemas/production","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"). Exit 0 = "},{"type":"text","value":"PASS prod healthy …","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"; non-zero writes a "},{"type":"text","value":"systemctl status","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" tail to stderr — read it, then "},{"type":"text","value":"journalctl $U -n 200 --no-pager","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"text","value":"$U","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" above), never retry blindly. After a deploy also tail "},{"type":"text","value":"journalctl $U -f","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" >=60 s for boot errors, supervisor restart loops, 5xx controllers."}]},{"id":"b9","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Operator one-shots"},{"id":"b10","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"barkpark.edges.backfill","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (and "},{"type":"text","value":"media.backfill","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"paper.backfill_block_ids","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"paper.composition_migrate","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":") boot a NARROWED tree ("},{"type":"text","value":"Barkpark.OneShot","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":") — no Endpoint, so an inherited "},{"type":"text","value":"PHX_SERVER","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" cannot bind the live slot’s port, as it did on guerrilla 2026-09-02 (“port 4001 already in use”). Mix still COMPILES. ON THE BOX, in "},{"type":"text","value":"/opt/barkpark","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"id":"b11","type":"code","value":"slot=$(systemctl is-active --quiet barkpark-slot@green && echo green || echo blue)\nset -a; . ./.env; . ./.slots/$slot.env; set +a  # unit env; sets MIX_BUILD_ROOT\ncd api && MIX_ENV=prod nice -n 19 mix barkpark.edges.backfill  # dry run"},{"id":"b12","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"MIX_BUILD_ROOT","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" must be the ACTIVE slot’s warm root with the checkout at its sha, or mix recompiles under the serving BEAM; "},{"type":"text","value":"nice","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" — that boot took the 2-core box from load 1.9 to 6.3. No "},{"type":"text","value":".slots/","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":": "},{"type":"text","value":". ./.env","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" alone, default "},{"type":"text","value":"_build","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":". Bare = dry run, "},{"type":"text","value":"--apply","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" writes."}]},{"id":"b13","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Prod migrations (validated live 2026-06-10)"},{"id":"b14","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"The hook DOES migrate: "},{"type":"text","value":"deploy-rebuild.sh","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" runs "},{"type":"text","value":"ecto.migrate","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" on new code while the old build serves, aborting the swap on failure (exit 13). By hand, keep that order — new code selecting an unmigrated column 500s every request:"}]},{"id":"b15","type":"code","value":"ssh root@89.167.28.206   # then ON THE BOX — never `&&`\ncd /opt/barkpark\nset -a; . ./.env; set +a  # backup: ecto:// -> postgresql://\npg_dump \"${DATABASE_URL/ecto:/postgresql:}\" | gzip > /root/pre-deploy.sql.gz\ngit checkout -- bin/barkpark bin/barkpark-pg go.sum  # dirt aborts the pull\ngit -c core.hooksPath=/dev/null pull --ff-only  # NO hook — old code serves on\nmake migrate              # start.sh mix ecto.migrate (ASDF + .env)\nbash .githooks/post-merge # rebuild + migrate + restart — SEE WARNING BELOW\n./api/scripts/prod-postcheck.sh"},{"id":"b16","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Destructive migrations (drop/rename) have no zero-downtime order — schedule a window: stop, migrate, deploy, start. Never "},{"type":"text","value":"make reset-db","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"text","value":"mix ecto.reset","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" on prod; a mid-way failure gets a forward fix, never an edit to an applied one."}]},{"id":"b17","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"The hook cannot report failure.","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" It exits 0 even when the rebuild fails (old build keeps serving), so "},{"type":"text","value":"prod-postcheck.sh","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" PASSes against that old build: grep it for "},{"type":"text","value":"WARN: deploy-rebuild failed","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":". A green postcheck proves the service is up, never that your code deployed. No-op on a "},{"type":"text","value":".slots","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (blue/green) box, which this host is not yet."}]},{"id":"b18","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Phoenix server rollback"},{"id":"b19","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Roll back by reverting source ("},{"type":"text","value":"git revert <bad-sha>","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", as a PR), never by resetting the server checkout; then on the box "},{"type":"text","value":"git pull","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"text","value":"./api/scripts/prod-postcheck.sh","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":". Never "},{"type":"text","value":"git reset --hard","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" or force-push the prod checkout; rebuild only via "},{"type":"text","value":"make rebuild","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (aside into "},{"type":"text","value":"api/_build_next","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", swaps on success) — never a hand-rolled partial clean, which serves stale BEAM/HEEx (Past Mistakes #1-3). Reverting code does NOT undo a schema change; write a compensating migration."}]},{"id":"b27","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Code anchors"},{"id":"b28","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"type":"text","value":"api/scripts/prod-postcheck.sh","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" — the postcheck"}],[{"type":"text","value":".githooks/post-merge","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" — rebuild + migrate + restart on server "},{"type":"text","value":"git pull","marks":["code"]}],[{"type":"text","value":"Makefile","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" — "},{"type":"text","value":"rebuild","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"text","value":"deploy","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"text","value":"migrate","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"text","value":"restart","marks":["code"]}],[{"type":"text","value":"api/start.sh","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" — systemd wrapper (ASDF + "},{"type":"text","value":".env","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":")"}]]}],"related":["ops-npm-rollback-playbook"]}
